@meta
id: 12-17
title: Scenario — the nightly payout sweep
chapter: 12
type: scenario
skills: search-slash, search-star, search-motion, search-offset
par: 75
minutes: 10
vscode: three round trips through Ctrl+F and a lot of scrolling
vimrc: set hlsearch incsearch
open: payout.sweep.task.ts

@brief
A ticket. One file, ninety lines, three unrelated fixes in it — which is
what a morning actually looks like.

    OPS-771  Payout sweep: paying out a hundredth of what it should,
             printing the ledger token into the logs, and retrying one
             time too many.

  1. The debug block at the top of `run` goes. All four lines of it,
     down to the `return`. One of them prints an API token into the
     application log, which is why this is a ticket and not a chore.

  2. The ledger counts in pence and `send` is handing it pounds. The
     amount passed to `ledgerService.record` needs multiplying by 100.

  3. `MAX_PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS` is a maximum, so a payout that has already
     used all of its attempts must not get another one. The comparison
     in `send` should be `>=`, not `>`.

Nothing else in the file changes. Do the whole thing without scrolling
and without a motion key that is not a search — the point of the exercise
is that you can navigate ninety lines by naming things.

@keys
| `/text` `Enter` | go to the next match |
| `d/text` `Enter` | delete from here to the next match |
| `/text/e` `Enter` | land on the last character of the match |
| `*` | search for the word under the cursor |
| `gg` | back to line 1 |
| `F` `x` `a` | back to a character on this line, then append |

@hints
Three jobs, three searches. Take them in file order and the cursor never
has to go backwards.
--
The debug block is an operator plus a search: start at its first line and
delete up to the `return`. The pence fix needs the cursor at the *end* of
what you find, which is what a search offset is for.
--
For the third fix, `MAX_PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS` is sitting on line 1 in the
import. Get the cursor onto it and press `*` rather than typing that
name out again — then `F>` and `a=`.

@solution
/const started<Enter>  d/return<Enter>
    /payout.amount/e<Enter>  a * 100<Esc>
    gg  fM  *  F>  a=<Esc>
    :wq<Enter>

Around sixty-five keystrokes for three fixes in a ninety-line file, and
not one of them was `j`, `k`, `G` or a scroll.

Look at the three moves and notice they are three different uses of the
same feature. The first uses a search as the *end* of an edit. The second
uses a search as a *destination with a precise landing spot*. The third
uses the text already under the cursor as the search itself, so a name
you would have had to type — and could have mistyped — never gets typed.

The one habit worth carrying out of this chapter is the first line of
that solution. When you know what you are looking for, say it. The file
being ninety lines or nine hundred stops being a fact you have to care
about, and the mouse stops being the obvious tool for "where is that
thing".

@start payout.sweep.task.ts
import { MAX_PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS } from '../../configuration/limits';
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { Task } from '../../infrastructure/task';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { PayoutRepository } from '../../domain/payout/payout.repository';
import { LedgerService } from '../../infrastructure/services/ledger.service';
import { AlertService } from '../../infrastructure/services/alert.service';

@injectable()
export class PayoutSweepTask extends Task {
  constructor(
    @inject(PayoutRepository) protected payoutRepository: PayoutRepository,
    @inject(LedgerService) protected ledgerService: LedgerService,
    @inject(AlertService) protected alertService: AlertService,
  ) {
    super();
  }

  public schedule = '0 3 * * *';

  public async run() {
    const started = Date.now();
    console.log('[payout-sweep] starting', new Date().toISOString());
    console.log('[payout-sweep] ledger token', process.env.LEDGER_API_TOKEN);
    console.log('[payout-sweep] elapsed ms', Date.now() - started);
    return this.sweep({ before: new Date() });
  }

  public async sweep(args: { before: Date }) {
    const due = await this.payoutRepository.findDue({ before: args.before });

    for (const payout of due) {
      await this.send(payout);
    }

    return { swept: due.length };
  }

  public async send(payout: { id: string; amount: number; attempts: number }) {
    if (payout.attempts > MAX_PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS) {
      await this.alertService.raise({
        channel: 'payments-oncall',
        message: `payout ${payout.id} exhausted its attempts`,
      });

      throw exception('PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED');
    }

    await this.ledgerService.record({
      reference: payout.id,
      amount: payout.amount,
      direction: 'CREDIT',
    });

    return this.payoutRepository.update({
      where: { id: payout.id },
      values: { status: 'SENT', sentAt: new Date() },
    });
  }

  public async onFailure(error: Error) {
    await this.alertService.raise({
      channel: 'payments-oncall',
      message: `payout sweep failed: ${error.message}`,
    });
  }
}

@expected payout.sweep.task.ts
import { MAX_PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS } from '../../configuration/limits';
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { Task } from '../../infrastructure/task';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { PayoutRepository } from '../../domain/payout/payout.repository';
import { LedgerService } from '../../infrastructure/services/ledger.service';
import { AlertService } from '../../infrastructure/services/alert.service';

@injectable()
export class PayoutSweepTask extends Task {
  constructor(
    @inject(PayoutRepository) protected payoutRepository: PayoutRepository,
    @inject(LedgerService) protected ledgerService: LedgerService,
    @inject(AlertService) protected alertService: AlertService,
  ) {
    super();
  }

  public schedule = '0 3 * * *';

  public async run() {
    return this.sweep({ before: new Date() });
  }

  public async sweep(args: { before: Date }) {
    const due = await this.payoutRepository.findDue({ before: args.before });

    for (const payout of due) {
      await this.send(payout);
    }

    return { swept: due.length };
  }

  public async send(payout: { id: string; amount: number; attempts: number }) {
    if (payout.attempts >= MAX_PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS) {
      await this.alertService.raise({
        channel: 'payments-oncall',
        message: `payout ${payout.id} exhausted its attempts`,
      });

      throw exception('PAYOUT_ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED');
    }

    await this.ledgerService.record({
      reference: payout.id,
      amount: payout.amount * 100,
      direction: 'CREDIT',
    });

    return this.payoutRepository.update({
      where: { id: payout.id },
      values: { status: 'SENT', sentAt: new Date() },
    });
  }

  public async onFailure(error: Error) {
    await this.alertService.raise({
      channel: 'payments-oncall',
      message: `payout sweep failed: ${error.message}`,
    });
  }
}
